From 612983bd5af72ceba65a2845659834b70b2c78fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:17:14 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 039/126] scripting: media events carry every field, the
 thumbnail's colours and the status

The host's media notifications now give scripts what SceneScript
documents, and reach text-layer scripts as well as property scripts:

- MediaPropertiesEvent has albumArtist, subTitle, genres and
  contentType (new wp_project_notify_track_metadata_extra; empty when
  unknown, contentType "music" by default), not only title, artist and
  albumTitle.
- MediaThumbnailEvent's colours come from the album art (a file://
  image): the most common colour and the next distinct ones, textColor
  with WCAG contrast >= 4.5 against the primary colour (else black or
  white), highContrastColor black or white, whichever contrasts more.
  WE's own extraction isn't decoded. hasThumbnail is whether the image
  loaded. The event fires when the image changes, not per track.
- mediaStatusChanged { enabled } (new wp_project_notify_media_status).
- What the host reported before the scene existed reaches the scripts
  on their first tick.
- wp_project_uses_media: whether the scene's scripts take media events
  (or it names $mediaThumbnail), so a host can skip reading the
  system's media sessions for the others.
- A replaced queued event is freed.

Origin: ours
Why: "now playing" widgets stayed empty (docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B10: S11-S14)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01288H8XbjUdhpEVfhFbe7bj
